Build's done and compiles clean. Summary of what changed:

- **`Config.java`** — added `JEV_API_KEY`, `JEV_BASE_URL` (default `https://api.typesafe.ai`), `JEV_MODEL` (default `jev-latest`), and `requireJevKey()`, checked only when the `jev` run is actually selected.
- **`ScoredAnswer.java`** — `correctness`/`faithfulness` widened from `int` to `double`, so Jev's probability-weighted score (e.g. `1.35`) passes through untouched.
- **`Scorer.java`** (new) — the interface `LlmJudgeScorer` and `TypeSafeJudgeScorer` both implement, so `BenchmarkRunner` doesn't care which judge it's holding.
- **`LlmJudgeScorer.java`** — now `implements Scorer`; `asInt` → `asDouble` (no behavior change, since it already returns clean integers).
- **`TypeSafeJudgeScorer.java`** (new) — calls Jev's `POST /v1/systemone` directly via `java.net.http.HttpClient` (no SDK dependency), sending `correctness`/`faithfulness` as typed `score` questions and refusal as a typed `noul` question, with manual exponential backoff on 429/529. `rationale` is always `""`, per your call.
- **`BenchmarkRunner.java`** — constructor now takes `Scorer`; print format and averaging widened to doubles.
- **`Main.java`** — new `-Dexec.args=jev` mode: GraphRAG retriever (same as default) + `TypeSafeJudgeScorer` instead of the OpenAI judge. Report/CSV filenames get a `-judge-jev` suffix. Critically: `jevJudge` only becomes `true` when `args[0]` is literally `"jev"` — the default (no arg) and `vector` runs are untouched and never touch Jev or require its key.
- **`env.sh`** — added a `JEV_API_KEY=...` placeholder for you to fill in when you're ready to try it.

Not touched: `pom.xml` (no new dependency needed) and `README.md` (didn't want to assume you want the docs updated yet — let me know if you'd like that too).